From f99f045ecab7747c5eb55ec414fba3444ec92ebd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 23:03:07 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(post,machine): Tormach microARC 4 - A indexing in
 the PathPilot post

A new machine file, Tormach 770MX + microARC 4, states an A rotary about
X (travel -360..360 degrees, rates unstated; TD10749). The PathPilot post
indexes A between operations: G53 G0 Z to the safe Z, then G0 A alone at a
section's first motion, and writes each indexed section's tips in the
turned frame (relative to the work offset, turned by -A about X). The A
word is read through the tool axis, so the pose law's A0 B180 posts as
A180. The direction sense is the sign of the rotary's axis vector. A
machine with an A states it at its first motion (A0 for upright work).

Refused by name: a tilt the A axis cannot reach (any X component, any
C), an A past the stated travel, an A that changes inside an operation
(simultaneous 4-axis - rollover and combined feed unconfirmed on
PathPilot, #796), an arc on an indexed A, and a tilt on a machine with no
A about X. No clamp code is written (none exists on the microARC 4).

Also fixes parse_mch's head search, which stopped at the first leaf part
and dropped the spindle, belt ranges and coolant of any file with a leaf
ahead of its head.

Adds the microARC hardware test kit (docs/tester-kits/tormach-microarc-4th:
README, the app-built project and its posted program, pinned by
microarc_test_part.rs).

Refs #785

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX
